%description:

Known deviation: Tr38901PathLossModel omits the 0.54 factor of the InH LOS
probability beyond 49 m.

3GPP TR 38.901 v16.1.0, Table 7.4.2-1, gives for Indoor - Open office

    P = 1                                     d2D <= 5 m
    P = exp(-(d2D - 5) / 70.8)                5 m < d2D <= 49 m
    P = 0.54 exp(-(d2D - 49) / 211.7)         d2D > 49 m

Tr38901PathLossModel::computeLosProbability() implements the third branch as
exp(-(d2D - 49) / 211.7) without the 0.54 factor. That makes the LOS
probability jump from 0.537 to 1.0 as the link crosses 49 m instead of
staying continuous, and overstates it by a factor 1.85 at every larger
distance.

The check below is the InH case left out of PathLossLosProbability.test.

%expected-failure: the InH LOS probability beyond 49 m is missing its 0.54 factor

%includes:
#include "PathLossTestUtil.h"
#include "simu5g/stack/phy/channelmodel/Tr38901PathLossModel.h"

%global:
using namespace simu5g;
using namespace simu5g::unittest;

%activity:
NumericChecker c(1e-8);
Tr38901PathLossModel m;
ScenarioParams p;

p = ScenarioParams();
p.scenario = INDOOR_HOTSPOT;
p.apply(m, this);

c.check("901 InH d2D=50",  m.computeLosProbability(50.1, 50, p.linkContext()),   0.537455236);
c.check("901 InH d2D=100", m.computeLosProbability(100.1, 100, p.linkContext()), 0.424393969);
c.check("901 InH d2D=200", m.computeLosProbability(200.1, 200, p.linkContext()), 0.264620213);

// The two branches meet at 49 m; without the factor the probability jumps.
c.check("901 InH continuous at 49 m",
        m.computeLosProbability(49.1, 49.0001, p.linkContext()) - m.computeLosProbability(48.9, 48.9999, p.linkContext()),
        0.0, 1e-5);

c.summary();

%contains: stdout
checks=4 failures=0

%not-contains: stdout
FAILED
